prompt:
A real photograph of the kitchen of an old family house in Kanazawa on an August morning, in a tall vertical picture, caught as it happens, as a relative at the kitchen door would take it with a good phone camera. Taken with a 24 mm lens at standing eye height from the doorway, looking across the kitchen towards the stove and the window above the sink, everything in sharp focus. Soft morning daylight from the window and steam from the pot; the textures of real worn wood, white enamel, stainless steel, ceramic, glass, steam, cotton cloth, food and skin.

The first reference picture shows the young woman from the front, the second shows her from her side, the third shows her grandmother Fumiko, a Japanese woman of eighty-two: the young woman's face, curly dark-brown hair and build, and Fumiko's face, short white hair and build, stay exactly as in them. Use them for the people only; here the young woman wears her white t-shirt and black jeans with a borrowed plain light-blue apron, and Fumiko a plain grey cardigan with a plain indigo apron.

Every surface in the picture is plain: the bottles of soy sauce and the jars are plain brown and plain white, the packets on the shelf are plain single colours, the walls are plain cream tiles and bare wood, the refrigerator is plain white, and the clock has a plain white face with two black hands. Each object stands clearly on its own, with a band of bare counter, bare wood or bare wall around it, so that the eye can tell at once where everything is.

The picture is built in three bands, from the bottom edge to the top edge.

THE FOREGROUND, along the bottom of the picture:
- the worn wooden floor of the kitchen;
- a small square wooden table on the left, set for breakfast: two bowls of white rice, a plate with two grilled fish, a small dish of yellow pickles, a bowl of raw eggs, two pairs of chopsticks on a small rest, and two white tea cups.

THE STOVE, across the middle of the picture:
- along the back, a long counter of stainless steel with a white enamel gas stove of two burners; on the front burner, a dented aluminium pot of miso soup steams, with cubes of white tofu and green spring onion floating in it;
- in front of the stove stands Fumiko of the third reference picture, small and upright, holding a wooden ladle in one hand, watching her granddaughter's face with a mischievous smile; her other hand, held behind her back where the camera sees it, hides a small plain orange paper packet of soup stock;
- beside her, on the right, the young woman of the reference pictures, in her apron, tastes the soup from the small bowl that she holds in both hands, her eyes closed, delighted;
- on the counter beside the stove: a wooden chopping board with a cut bunch of spring onions and a knife laid flat beside it, a block of white tofu on a plate, a brown earthenware jar of miso paste with its lid off, a bottle of soy sauce, and small jars of sugar and salt;
- on the right, a white refrigerator with a few small magnets of plain colours on its door.

THE BACK OF THE KITCHEN, across the upper third of the picture:
- above the sink, a wide window with a wooden frame, half open, with the green leaves of a persimmon tree outside;
- on the windowsill, a small glass of water with a sprig of green leaves in it;
- on the left wall, open wooden shelves with stacks of rice bowls, plates and tea cups, and a round wall clock with a black rim;
- a single round lamp with a white glass shade hangs from the dark wooden ceiling.

The kitchen is old, warm and lived-in: between the objects and the people, the same bare wood, the same bare counter and the same plain cream tiles.
